@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-5">

    <div class="mb-5">
        <span class="text-uppercase fw-bold"
              style="color: var(--raceday-orange); letter-spacing: 2px;">
            RACEDAY • YOUR INFORMATION
        </span>

        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mt-2">
            Privacy Policy
        </h1>

        <p class="text-muted">
            Your privacy matters. This page explains how RaceDay
            collects, uses and handles information when you use
            our platform.
        </p>

        <small class="text-muted">
            Last updated: November 2026
        </small>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">1. Information We Collect</h4>

            <p>
                RaceDay collects information that is necessary to
                provide its event management and participation
                services. This may include:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>First name and last name.</li>
                <li>Email address and phone number.</li>
                <li>Date of birth.</li>
                <li>Account type, such as Organiser or Participant.</li>
                <li>Profile pictures uploaded to your account.</li>
                <li>Event enrolment and participation information.</li>
                <li>Race results and finishing positions.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">2. How We Use Your Information</h4>

            <p>
                Information collected through RaceDay is used to:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Create and manage user accounts.</li>
                <li>Authenticate users and provide role-based access.</li>
                <li>Allow organisers to create and manage sporting events.</li>
                <li>Allow participants to browse and enrol in events.</li>
                <li>Track event enrolments and participation statuses.</li>
                <li>Record and display race results.</li>
                <li>Display account information and profile pictures.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">3. Event Participation Information</h4>

            <p>
                When participants enrol in events, information
                relating to their enrolment may be made available
                to the relevant event organiser.
            </p>

            <p>
                Organisers use this information to manage
                participants, monitor enrolments and record
                race results.
            </p>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">4. Profile Pictures and Uploaded Content</h4>

            <p>
                RaceDay allows users to upload profile pictures
                and event organisers to upload event banner images.
                These images are stored using cloud-based storage
                services integrated with the application.
            </p>

            <p>
                Uploaded images are used to support the visual
                features of the platform, including user profiles
                and event listings.
            </p>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">5. Data Security</h4>

            <p>
                RaceDay uses authentication and role-based access
                controls to restrict access to application
                functionality according to user roles.
            </p>

            <p>
                The application also uses controlled API access
                and cloud-based storage services when handling
                application data and uploaded images.
            </p>

            <p>
                While reasonable measures are used to protect
                information, no online system can guarantee
                absolute security.
            </p>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">6. Data Retention</h4>

            <p>
                Account, event, enrolment and results information
                is maintained as part of the application's
                operational records.
            </p>

            <p>
                This policy does not specify a fixed retention
                period. Information handling is subject to the
                application's data management practices.
            </p>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0 mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">7. Your Responsibilities</h4>

            <ul>
                <li>Provide accurate information when registering.</li>
                <li>Keep your account credentials confidential.</li>
                <li>Only upload appropriate profile pictures and images.</li>
                <li>Notify the appropriate administrator if you
                    believe your account has been accessed without
                    authorisation.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <h4 class="fw-bold">8. Contact and Enquiries</h4>

            <p class="mb-0">
                If you have questions or concerns about the
                information associated with your RaceDay account,
                please contact the platform administrator.
            </p>

        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-5">
        <p class="text-muted small">
            RACE<span style="color: var(--raceday-orange);">DAY</span>
            &copy; 2026. All rights reserved.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>